{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1147462-my-first-cofd-campaign-idea-and-questions","id":1147462,"title":"My first CofD campaign Idea and Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-06T09:23:46-07:00","id":1147462,"title":"My first CofD campaign Idea and Questions","content":"So I have run several campaigns using the OWoD and V20 rules but this is my first foray into the NWoD/CoD setting.<br /> Still coming to grip with the differences but I think I'm good for the most part.<br /> <br /> My campaign is going to be set during the 1970's in Philadelphia.<br /> The players will be part of a supernatural detective agency (think ghostbusters).<br /> I want the story to be lead by the players themselves for the most part; I do plan on having an overarching plot and antagonists but I don't want to control how they progress.<br /> I plan on keeping them on their toes in that some of the jobs they will take on whilst seeming supernatural will actually be quite mundane (scoobydoo villains) and others will take a wtf turn into the god machine territory.<br /> <br /> My biggest questions are really about the system.<br /> How are the merits and the supernatural merits in general? Are they game breaking for a chronicle with human players?<br /> Is there anything I should forbid during character creation in general or caution players against so that they don't end up with twinked out mary-sues? or is that not even an issue? (one problem I always had with OWoD was the massive dice pools some players would generate by super specifying their characters)<br /> Anything I should do to speed up combat? with OWoD I would ditch the declaration phase entirely since it just ate up time (unless is a important interaction with named villains) and reduce the mooks health so they died faster.<br /> Also how compatible are other splats with the new CoD book? Mainly MtA 2e and VtR 2e and PtC 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2500,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic","user":"Corelogic","date":". 10-06-2017, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic","name":"Corelogic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T10:01:00-07:00","id":1147471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corelogic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1147462-my-first-cofd-campaign-idea-and-questions#post1147462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are the merits and the supernatural merits in general? Are they game breaking for a chronicle with human players?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. If anything I recommend getting the book Hurt Locker as well since it contains additional Supernatural Merits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corelogic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1147462-my-first-cofd-campaign-idea-and-questions#post1147462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything I should forbid during character creation in general or caution players against so that they don't end up with twinked out mary-sues? or is that not even an issue? (one problem I always had with OWoD was the massive dice pools some players would generate by super specifying their characters)</div> </div> </div> </div>As a human it's a bit difficult reaching massive attack dice pools. The best ways to do it is to have Professional Training 5 in order to gain Rote Action on your attacks for a WP point, and having several overlapping Specialties (along with the Merit Area of Expertise) on the chosen fighting Skill.<br /> Ways to avoid such dice pools are to houserule that Professional Training 5 doesn't apply to attack rolls (my group has houseruled that away because in late game it's crippling <i>not</i> to have your chosen fighting Skill as an asset skill), limit how many dots the players may place in Skills at character creation, and simply saying no to Specialty combinations that will overlap most or all of the time, as well as saying no to Specialties that are too wide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corelogic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1147462-my-first-cofd-campaign-idea-and-questions#post1147462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything I should do to speed up combat? with OWoD I would ditch the declaration phase entirely since it just ate up time (unless is a important interaction with named villains) and reduce the mooks health so they died faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't played oWoD, but from what I've heard the combat in CofD takes just a fraction of the time it did in oWoD. Even if I'm ill informed the combat is pretty quick. You roll initiative once, and most of the time each attack is only a single roll. The attack dice pool is modified by difficulty to hit, and the result of the roll is modified by the weapon and the opponents armour to see how much and what type of damage is dealt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corelogic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1147462-my-first-cofd-campaign-idea-and-questions#post1147462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also how compatible are other splats with the new CoD book? Mainly MtA 2e and VtR 2e and PtC 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're compatible rules-wise (since every line uses the same system), but not necessarily thematically. There can also be uncertainties in how different supernatural abilities interact with each other, but it's not a prohibitive problem. And any directly opposing supernatural powers are resolved through the Clash of Wills rule, so no problem there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-06-2017, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}